+### The 7 Invalidity Classes
 
-1. Navigate to `/admin/diagnostics` in the web application using an account with `SERVER_ADMIN` credentials.
-2. Verify that all status indicators in the Subsystem Overview grid display **Operational** (`green`).
-3. Click **Run Health Probe** to execute active roundtrip latency measurements against the database, outbox relay, and WebSocket hub.
-4. Review the **Migration State** card to confirm 76/76 migrations are applied with single-head consistency.
-5. If any subsystem reports **Degraded** or **Down**, click **Inspect Subsystem** to view raw exception logs and performance percentiles.
+The Link Auditor (`POST /api/v1/admin/object-links:audit`) evaluates every link against 7 formal invalidity classes:
 
-### Link Graph Remediation Procedure
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+    Scan["Integrity Audit Scan (POST /api/v1/admin/object-links:audit)"] --> C1["1. DANGLING_SOURCE - Source object UUID missing from PostgreSQL"]
+    Scan --> C2["2. DANGLING_TARGET - Target object UUID missing from PostgreSQL"]
+    Scan --> C3["3. SOFT_DELETED_ENDPOINT - Endpoint object soft-deleted past retention window"]
+    Scan --> C4["4. ARCHIVED_POLICY_VIOLATION - Link between active and archived entities violating policy"]
+    Scan --> C5["5. TYPE_MATRIX_VIOLATION - Link kind forbidden between endpoint object types"]
+    Scan --> C6["6. CROSS_WORKSPACE_LEAK - Cross-workspace link violating multi-tenant boundary"]
+    Scan --> C7["7. PERMISSION_SEVERED - Principal lacks access across endpoint boundary"]
+```
 
-1. Switch to the **Link Inspector** tab or navigate directly to `/admin/link-auditor`.
-2. Click **Start Comprehensive Scan** (`GET /api/v1/admin/link-auditor/scan`).
-3. Review the defect summary cards grouped by defect class (`ORPHAN_SOURCE`, `ORPHAN_TARGET`, `CROSS_WORKSPACE`, etc.).
-4. Click on any row to open the **Forensic Inspection Drawer** and review the link metadata.
-5. Click **Purge Invalid Links** to open the remediation modal.
-6. Review the calculated blast radius. Type the confirmation phrase `PURGE INVALID LINKS` and confirm.
-7. Verify that the operation completes successfully and inspect the updated link audit counter (expected: 0 defects).
+1. **`DANGLING_SOURCE`:** The link record specifies a `source_id` entity that no longer exists in the universal objects spine.
+2. **`DANGLING_TARGET`:** The link record specifies a `target_id` entity that has been hard-deleted or does not exist in the database.
+3. **`SOFT_DELETED_ENDPOINT`:** One or both endpoints of the link reference an object soft-deleted beyond the workspace retention threshold.
+4. **`ARCHIVED_POLICY_VIOLATION`:** The link connects an active entity to an archived entity in violation of project archiving policy.
+5. **`TYPE_MATRIX_VIOLATION`:** The relation violates the registered link type matrix allowlist (valid kinds: `BLOCKS`, `BLOCKED_BY`, `RELATES_TO`, `PARENT_OF`, `CHILD_OF`, `DUPLICATES`, `DUPLICATED_BY`, `PROMOTED_TO`, `PROMOTED_FROM`, `MENTIONS`, `REFERENCED_IN`, `ATTACHED_TO`, `DERIVED_FROM`).
+6. **`CROSS_WORKSPACE_LEAK`:** The link connects two entities across distinct workspace tenant boundaries without an active federation agreement, violating multi-tenant isolation.
+7. **`PERMISSION_SEVERED`:** The link endpoints span access boundaries where caller or entity permissions have been revoked or severed.
 
