+### 1. Streaming Direct Download (`KBKP` Format)
+- **Endpoint:** `POST /api/v1/admin/standalone/backup`
+- **Mechanism:** Streams an AES-256-GCM encrypted payload directly to the operator's web browser without buffering the full archive on server disk.
+- **Envelope Header:** 34-byte binary header: `KBKP` (4 bytes magic) + `version` (`1`, 1 byte) + `kdf_mode` (`1`=PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 600,000 iterations, `2`=HKDF-SHA256, 1 byte) + `salt` (16 bytes) + `nonce` (12 bytes), followed by the AES-256-GCM ciphertext stream of raw `pg_dump --format=custom` bytes terminated with a 16-byte authentication tag.
+- **Passphrase Contract:** Derived via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 with 600,000 iterations. Passphrases must be at least 16 characters in length.
 
-![System Settings and Environment Configuration](images/26-system-settings.png)
+### 2. Server-Side Automated Snapshots (`KBBAK1` Format)
+- **Endpoint:** `POST /api/v1/admin/standalone/backups/run-now`
+- **Daemon Privilege Separation:** Managed by a dedicated, root-privileged local daemon communicating strictly over UNIX domain socket `/run/postgresql/.kb_ops.sock` (mode `0660`, group `65532`). The web application process running as non-root user `kanban_app` cannot directly invoke shell scripts or bypass database controls; it issues fixed-operation JSON-line IPC commands (`"pg_dump_raw"`, `"restore_backup"`, `"scheduled_backup"`).
+- **Storage Location:** Saved in `/var/lib/kanban/data/backups` with ISO-8601 timestamps (e.g. `kanban-backup-20261125T144207Z.kbbak`).
+- **Archive Structure:** Tar archive prefixed with 37-byte header `KBBAK1\x00\x01` using Argon2id (`KDF_MODE_ARGON2ID` with 64 MiB memory, time=3, parallelism=4) or `KDF_MODE_RAW`, encrypting 4 MiB AES-256-GCM chunks of a tar bundle containing `manifest.json`, `database.pgdump`, `attachments/`, and optional `secrets_carryover.json`.
+
+![Standalone Backups and Snapshot History](images/slice4-standalone-backups-snapshot-history.png)
 
